  "result": "Fixed. `IntRange` with `clamp=True` and an open bound now clamps to the value just inside the range.\n\n**The bug:** in `src/click/types.py`, `IntRange._clamp` returned `bound - dir` for open bounds. For `IntRange(0, 5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` and input `10`, `dir` is -1, so the result was `5 - (-1) = 6`, which is outside the range. The lower bound was wrong the same way: `min_open` with input `-1` returned `-1`.\n\n**The fix:** changed it to `bound + dir`, so the results are `4` for the max case and `1` for the min case.\n\n**Tests:** added two cases to `tests/test_types.py`:\n- `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"-1\"` \u2192 `1`\n- `IntRange(0, 5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"10\"` \u2192 `4`\n\n`pytest tests/test_types.py` passes (43 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't run the full suite.\n\nI didn't touch `FloatRange`. It rejects clamping with open bounds at construction, so the bug doesn't apply there. I also didn't add a changelog entry in `docs/changes.md`; say if you want one.",
